From: DevilSmove <3363025686@qq.com>
Subject: [PATCH] mtd: spinand: stop probing when required NMBM attach fails

A device declaring mediatek,nmbm uses logical offsets from the NMBM
mapping. Registering its raw NAND partitions after an attach failure can
expose different offsets and permit writes to unrelated physical blocks.

Keep the existing behavior for devices not declaring NMBM, but fail the
probe before registering partitions when a required map cannot be loaded.

Signed-off-by: DevilSmove <3363025686@qq.com>
---
--- a/drivers/mtd/nand/spi/core.c
+++ b/drivers/mtd/nand/spi/core.c
@@ -1675,7 +1675,15 @@
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
 
-	mtk_bmt_attach(mtd);
+	ret = mtk_bmt_attach(mtd);
+	if (ret && of_property_read_bool(mtd_get_of_node(mtd),
+					 "mediatek,nmbm")) {
+		dev_err(&mem->spi->dev,
+			"Required NMBM attach failed (%d); refusing raw MTD fallback\n",
+			ret);
+		goto err_spinand_cleanup;
+	}
+
 	ret = mtd_device_register(mtd, NULL, 0);
 	if (ret)
 		goto err_spinand_cleanup;
